Sure, a loop is a way of repeating a block of code a certain number of times.  For example, here’s a simple loop that prints the numbers from 1 to 10:

for (int i = 1; i <= 10; i++) {
    cout << i << endl;
}

This code will print the numbers from 1 to 10, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, and 10.  There are many different kinds of loops, and in C you can use for loops, while loops, and do-while loops.  I recommend reading the documentation for your programming language to learn more about the different kinds of loops.

